description:
globals.css doesn't set -webkit-tap-highlight-color, so iOS Safari paints the default translucent gray rectangle on every tap (looks unprofessional for an app-like surface). It also doesn't set -webkit-text-size-adjust, so iOS will sometimes inflate body text on landscape rotation, breaking layout.

Fix:
- html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100% }
- * { -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent }

Don't set -webkit-touch-callout: none globally — users still expect long-press save-image / copy-link.
